owers"},{"surface":"மலையவும்","parts":[{"text":"மலைய","lemma":"மலைய","gloss":"to wear as a wreath"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and to wear"},{"surface":"புலவர்","parts":[{"text":"புலவர்","lemma":"புலவர்","gloss":"poets"}],"gloss":"poets"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூநுதல்","parts":[{"text":"பூ","lemma":"பூ","gloss":"beauty"},{"text":"நுதல்","lemma":"நுதல்","gloss":"forehead"}],"gloss":"beautiful forehead"},{"surface":"யானையோடு","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"},{"text":"ஓடு","lemma":"ஓடு","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with elephants"},{"surface":"புனைதேர்","parts":[{"text":"புனை","lemma":"புனை","gloss":"decorated"},{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"தேர்","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"decorated chariots"},{"surface":"பண்ணவும்","parts":[{"text":"பண்ணவும்","lemma":"பண்ணவும்","gloss":"and to equip"}],"gloss":"and to equip","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அறனோ","parts":[{"text":"அறன்","lemma":"அறன்","gloss":"righteousness"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"is it"}],"gloss":"is it righteous"},{"surface":"மற்றஇது","parts":[{"text":"மற்றஇது","lemma":"மற்றஇது","gloss":"then this"}],"gloss":"then this","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"விறல்மாண்","parts":[{"text":"விறல்","lemma":"விறல்","gloss":"victory"},{"text":"மாண்","lemma":"மாண்","gloss":"glorious"}],"gloss":"glorious in victory"},{"surface":"குடுமி","parts":[{"text":"குடுமி","lemma":"குடுமி","gloss":"Kudumi"}],"gloss":"O Kudumi"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இன்னா","parts":[{"text":"இன்னா","lemma":"இன்னா","gloss":"misery"}],"gloss":"misery"},{"surface":"ஆகப்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகப்","lemma":"ஆகப்","gloss":"to happen"}],"gloss":"to happen","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிறர்","parts":[{"text":"பிறர்","lemma":"பிறர்","gloss":"others"}],"gloss":"others'"},{"surface":"மண்","parts":[{"text":"மண்","lemma":"மண்","gloss":"land"}],"gloss":"land"},{"surface":"கொண்டு","parts":[{"text":"கொண்டு","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"having taken"}],"gloss":"having seized"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இனிய","parts":[{"text":"இனிய","lemma":"இனிது","gloss":"pleasant things"}],"gloss":"pleasant things"},{"surface":"செய்தி","parts":[{"text":"செய்தி","lemma":"செய்","gloss":"you do"}],"gloss":"you do"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"ஆர்வலர்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்வலர்","lemma":"ஆர்வலர்","gloss":"well-wishers"}],"gloss":"well-wishers"},{"surface":"முகத்தே","parts":[{"text":"முகத்தே","lemma":"முகத்தே","gloss":"on the faces"}],"gloss":"on the faces","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"bards lotus to wear as a wreath and poets / with elephants having beautiful foreheads decorated chariots to equip and / is it righteous then this O Kudumi of glorious victory / misery to happen others' land having seized / pleasant things you do on the faces of your well-wishers","translation":"While bards wear golden lotuses and poets harness decorated chariots drawn by elephants with beautiful foreheads, is it righteous, O Kudumi of glorious victory, that you bring misery to others by seizing their lands, while bringing joy to the faces of those who love you?","modern":"பாணர்கள் பொன்னாலான தாமரை மலர்களைச் சூடவும், புலவர்கள் அழகிய நெற்றியையுடைய யானைகளோடு அலங்கரிக்கப்பட்ட தேர்களைச் செலுத்தவும் பரிசுகளை வழங்குகிறாய். வெற்றி பொருந்திய பெருமைமிக்க குடுமியே! பிறருடைய நாடுகளைக் கைப்பற்றி அவர்களுக்குத் துன்பத்தை உண்டாக்கி, உன்னை விரும்புவோரின் முகங்களில் மகிழ்ச்சியானவற்றைச் செய்வது உனக்கு அறமாகுமோ?","explanation":"The poet Neṭṭimaiyār addresses the Pāṇṭiya king Palyākasālai Mutukuṭumip Peruvaḻuti in this poem of the pāṭāṇ tiṇai (praise of a king). He employs a beautiful irony, questioning whether the king's actions are righteous. On one hand, the king is immensely generous, gifting golden lotuses to bards and elephants and chariots to poets, bringing joy to his well-wishers. On the other hand, he ruthlessly conquers the lands of his enemies, bringing them great misery. By asking \"is this righteous?\", the poet praises the king's dual nature of being extremely kind to his subjects and devastatingly fierce to his foes. Key words include 'pāṇar' (bards), 'pulavar' (poets), 'aṟaṉō' (is it righteous?), and 'kuṭumi' (the king's name).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}